        "source_behavior": "Pinned FreeType accepts malformed public BDF numeric property tokens through bdf_atol_ and bdf_atoul_: no digits become zero, trailing non-digits are ignored, and overflowing prefixes saturate.",
        "expansion_reason": "Source review found a real parity mismatch: Rust used all-or-nothing parse::<i64/u64>(), dropping the property, while FreeType stores the permissively parsed numeric value. These 30 inputs distinguish no-value, no-digit, signed, decimal-prefix, saturation, and cardinal cases before and after the fix."
      },
      "expectation": {
        "status": "ok",
        "output_shape": {
          "return": "FT_Error",
          "record": "BDF_PropertyRec",
          "union_fields": ["atom", "integer", "cardinal"]
        },
